50. Qg6+ Kg8 51. Qxc6 Rf6 52. Qe8+ { Initially, it might seem that the Rook can oscillate between f6 and h6 indefinitely. But working through the three questions, we find that there is a way for White to force zugzwang. } Kh7 53. Kxg4 Rh6 54. Kf4 Rf6 55. Ke5 Rh6 56. Qe6 { Black cannot routinely play ...Rf6 because of Qxf6. ...Kh8 does not work either because of Qxh6, where White wins the resulting endgame } Rf6 ( 56... Rxe6 57. fxe6 Kg8 58. Kd6 g5 59. e7 Kf7 60. Kd7 ) 
 ( 56... Rf6 57. Qxf6 gxf6 58. Kxf6 Kg8 59. Ke7 ) 
