 { This is a game between Maxime Vachier-Lagrave (White) and Sam Shankland (Black) . What are some possible goals and how do we work towards them? } 1... { -KEY- } Kxb4 $1 2. Kd4 Nc6+ $1 3. Kxd5 Kc3 $3 { The only way White can win is by promoting the two pawns. They are currently fixed on dark squares. This means they cannot be defended by the light-squared Bishop. Therefore, the only goal is to activate our King and attack those pawns. Nothing else matters, not even our Knight. } 4. Kxc6 { The c6 Knight stopped both Ke5 and Ke6 } ( 4. Ke6 Nd4 ) 
Kd2 5. Bc4 Ke3 { The White pawns are helpless on dark squares } 6. Bg8 Kxf4 7. Bxh7 Kxg5 { Shankland managed to clinch half a point from this game because he recognised that White's pawns were weak on dark squares, and all that he needed to do is activate the King. The Knight could have attacked the pawns but 2...Ne6 would be well met by 3. Ke5 } 
