 { Black is forking both our Bishops. How should we deal with that? } 1. { -KEY- } Bg2 $3 Rxf4+ 2. Kg3 { The Rook is trapped because the Knight singularly controls both light and dark squares. If the Black Rook moves to a light square, the White Knight is ready to move away from b7 to create a discovered check while attacking the light square that the Rook is on If the Black Rook moves to a dark square, the b7 Knight will move to a dark square and give a discovered check. Black will be forced to move his King to b8, a dark square. With both the Rook and King on a dark square, as well as our Knight ready to hop to a light square, we will have a Knight fork. } Rf8 ( 2... Rf7 3. Nd6 Kb8 4. Nxf7 ) 
